#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:5 736b33be59e34c9fa85565bcb78afbbc
msgid "ZigZag Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:7 9393f174ef994e1e843ad7d3de24bdda
msgid ""
"ZigZag mode is a semi-autonomous mode designed to make it easier for a "
"pilot to fly a vehicle back and forth across a field which can be useful "
"for crop spraying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:12 5a225c07920849deb8488429ee3f7acc
msgid "The way it works is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:14 c91b8348997948e7a3ac01e66d7b2c39
msgid ""
"A two or three position :ref:`auxiliary switch <channel-7-and-8-options>`"
" is set to 61 / \"ZigZag SaveWP\" (i.e. :ref:`RC7_OPTION <RC7_OPTION>` = "
"61)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:15 4e24641a060d4295a976e310aaea9ff9
msgid ""
"The pilot arms the vehicle and takes off.  The vehicle will fly just like"
" :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:16 991cd78497a7439faa22c6d00a7687dc
msgid ""
"The vehicle is flown manually to one side of the field and then the "
"auxiliary switch is moved to the highest or lowest position (it doesn't "
"matter which) to record that side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:17 143722045ebb40599d8a79bff749668d
msgid ""
"The vehicle is flown to the other side of the field and the switch is "
"moved to the opposite position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:18 11857dce9bfa43e5ac131790af30d225
msgid ""
"The switch can now be used to start the vehicle flying autonomously (at "
"the current height) to either side of the field.  Once the vehicle "
"reaches the other side it will revert to manual control.  The pilot can "
"also regain manual control by moving the auxiliary switch to the middle "
"position or by changing the flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:19 1ccd8c3048594cd9856f255a43395b95
msgid ""
"If a downward facing :ref:`range finder <common-rangefinder-landingpage>`"
" is used, the vehicle will follow the terrain when flying.  If the range "
"finder becomes unhealthy while traversing from one side to the other, the"
" vehicle will revert to manual control and come to a stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:25 c9b42fb5b9884651bedca193a85ec191
msgid ""
"When flown manually ZigZag uses :ref:`Loiter mode's <loiter-mode>`  "
"parameters.  For example the top speed can be configured with "
":ref:`LOIT_SPEED <LOIT_SPEED>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:27 396b8fbb5c7f4816a1be71c227fcce28
msgid ""
"When autonomously flying from one side of the field to the other, the "
":ref:`Auto mode <auto-mode>` parameters are used.  For example the top "
"speed can be configured with :ref:`WPNAV_SPEED <WPNAV_SPEED>`.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:32 6820248d2e2b41639d37cfda55332388
msgid "Automatic Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:34 d974ce97544141f7aee84cae3c2ea97c
msgid "This feature will be available in Copter-4.1.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:36 8c74c119ccf64ab397e89815d171ad4c
msgid ""
"this function must be enabled with "
":ref:`ZIGZ_AUTO_ENABLE<ZIGZ_AUTO_ENABLE>` = 1, and parameters reloaded, "
"before any parameters are visible and the feature enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:38 1264e6f1f3c64dc5a5a2004fc7bfa39e
msgid ""
"After the field's side points are registered, if you have an RC switch "
"configured with ``RCx_OPTION`` = 83 (ZigZag Auto Mode), you can "
"automatically cover the field side to side at a programmable distance "
"interval, also enabling a sprayer, if equipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:43 8a021b8d56e14ee990e2d8b1666d4448
msgid "To use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:45 e0369b839b954506bf08de7a238c91bb
msgid ""
"Fly to one side of the field and register the ZigZagWP A, as above, then "
"fly to ZigZagWP B and set it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:46 9a7193a70bd145efa749c2e5e2bc1326
msgid ""
"Then switch the ZigZag Auto Mode switch you had setup. The vehicle will "
"proceed as shown in the diagram, automatically enabling a sprayer, if "
"setup. See :ref:`sprayer` for instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:47 88e90901328b4760ab902d1ba108ce13
msgid ""
"Upon activation, the vehicle will move in "
":ref:`ZIGZ_DIRECTION<ZIGZ_DIRECTION>` with respect to its heading for "
":ref:`ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST<ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST>`, then proceed to cross the field "
"until the opposite ZigZagWP is reached. It will then wait for "
":ref:`ZIGZ_WP_DELAY<ZIGZ_WP_DELAY>` to allow sprayer to fully stop and "
"then move :ref:`ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST<ZIGZ_SIDE_DIST>` down the side of the "
"field again to proceed back across the area. It will do this for "
":ref:`ZIGZ_LINE_NUM<ZIGZ_LINE_NUM>` times (-1 = infinite until switched "
"out of this mode, =0 will only move to the first field crossing position,"
" but not proceed further)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/zigzag-mode.rst:49 423f2aa30c6b4d32b31726647279f648
msgid ""
"Moving the ZigZag Auto switch to the low position immediately stops this "
"mode and returns to normal ZIGZAG mode."
msgstr ""

